\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Log--log plot of wall-clock time per force evaluation versus particle count $N$ for brute-force $O(N^2)$, symmetric-pair, and Barnes--Hut tree methods. The brute-force quadratic scaling is confirmed by the slope $\approx 2$ on the log--log plot. The Barnes--Hut tree shows sub-quadratic scaling but high constant factors from Python recursion overhead. \relax }}{10}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scaling}{{3}{10}{Log--log plot of wall-clock time per force evaluation versus particle count $N$ for brute-force $O(N^2)$, symmetric-pair, and Barnes--Hut tree methods. The brute-force quadratic scaling is confirmed by the slope $\approx 2$ on the log--log plot. The Barnes--Hut tree shows sub-quadratic scaling but high constant factors from Python recursion overhead. \relax }{figure.caption.11}{}}
